+You tap once to start or resume a recording, and it can stop without a second tap:
+* **Start**:
+the first tap starts recording when the prompt input is empty, so you can still type spaces normally while composing a message.
+To add to a recording that stopped by itself, [resume it](#resume-a-recording-that-stopped-by-itself).
+recording also stops when you send or edit the prompt.
+It stops by itself after 60 seconds with no recognized words or after 10 minutes total.
+### Resume a recording that stopped by itself When a tap-mode recording stops by itself, your words stay in the prompt unsent and the footer says why.
+You can send the words, or add to them if you haven't edited them:
+* **Send the words**:
+press `Enter`.
+* **Add to the words**:
+put the cursor at the end of the words and tap `Space` to record again.
+When you tap again to stop, Claude Code sends all of the text if you added at least three words.
+To see what stopped the recording, find the part of the footer message that starts with `dictation stopped`:
